,"source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:edcef2babb056bfc685107a6bc5f44d1b622a17a6a6e7862e5dddcf337d48e01","file":"preprints/Hardness-of-finding-large-independent-sets-in-three-colorable-graphs-September-24-2026/build/source/sections/introduction.tex","line":12,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"1c61ee34a2e5ffcb1eb9c36739825a34bbd0424c6c18b9ac8760d7980a26a43a","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Hardness-of-finding-large-independent-sets-in-three-colorable-graphs-September-24-2026/build/source/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:edcef2babb056bfc685107a6bc5f44d1b622a17a6a6e7862e5dddcf337d48e01","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Hardness-of-finding-large-independent-sets-in-three-colorable-graphs-September-24-2026/build/source/sections/introduction.tex#L12"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nFor every fixed real $0<\\delta<1/3$, there is a deterministic\npolynomial-time algorithm $R_\\delta$ that maps each explicitly encoded\nBoolean $3$-CNF formula $\\phi$ to a nonempty finite simple undirected\nunweighted graph $G_\\phi$ such that\n\\[\n \\begin{array}{ll}\n \\phi\\text{ is satisfiable}\n   &\\Longrightarrow G_\\phi\\text{ is three-colorable},\\\\[2pt]\n \\phi\\text{ is unsatisfiable}\n   &\\Longrightarrow \\alpha(G_\\phi)<\\delta\\,|V(G_\\phi)|.\n \\end{array}\n\\]\nThe running time and explicit output size are polynomial in the ordinary\nbinary encoding length of $\\phi$. Their constants and polynomial degree\nmay depend on the fixed $\\delta$, but not on $\\phi$.\nThe coloring in the first implication covers every vertex and is not\nsupplied with the graph."}
